{"lines":[{"c":1,"y":0.072674418306663879,"t":"Test 2","w":0.058270676930745446,"h":0.015988372635703185,"x":0.1710526313685872},{"t":"READING","h":0.018895348808647294,"c":1,"y":0.12063953487910661,"x":0.49999999849904481,"w":0.12593985239664712},{"x":0.16917293481946102,"y":0.18158403100163079,"w":0.29135337829589847,"h":0.018997364326668653,"t":"READING PASSAGE 1","c":1},{"w":0.765223388671875,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading","y":0.21884988768612601,"x":0.17095928427049331,"h":0.023228009746524503,"c":1},{"w":0.16048107147216797,"t":"Passage 1 below.","h":0.021824251507761017,"x":0.16882328246890996,"c":1,"y":0.23673186221613463},{"w":0.38563830057779952,"c":1,"h":0.024992007558298335,"t":"Bringing cinnamon to Europe","x":0.37014418803397137,"y":0.27753152206637699},{"c":1,"w":0.76891560872395837,"h":0.020001496795831075,"y":0.31822392776198694,"t":"Cinnamon is a sweet, fragrant spice produced from the inner bark of trees of the genus","x":0.16910909614138991},{"c":1,"w":0.78209086100260428,"h":0.020816466459825711,"t":"Cinnamomum, which is native to the Indian sub-continent. It was known in biblical times,","x":0.16910841514153038,"y":0.33531346219495417},{"h":0.020255739736464995,"c":1,"t":"and is mentioned in several books of the Bible, both as an ingredient that was mixed","x":0.16721569648390311,"y":0.35449197029091917,"w":0.74639806111653639},{"y":0.37004694143706751,"c":1,"h":0.025820489553044945,"t":"with oils for anointing people's bodies, and also as a token indicating friendship among","w":0.76541147867838533,"x":0.167116348270818},{"y":0.39095060020456429,"w":0.74453831990559904,"h":0.020658973256619029,"x":0.16531423919378796,"t":"lovers and friends. In ancient Rome, mourners attending funerals burnt cinnamon to","c":1},{"w":0.73515630086263017,"h":0.020612026443039166,"t":"create a pleasant scent. Most often, however, the spice found its primary use as an","c":1,"x":0.16719377053676718,"y":0.40863437377990608},{"y":0.42719929556794645,"t":"additive to food and drink. In the Middle Ages, Europeans who could afford the spice","w":0.74639729817708345,"c":1,"h":0.020432859102680334,"x":0.16721087569633056},{"y":0.44622093023757681,"x":0.16729324270696555,"t":"used it to flavour food, particularly meat, and to impress those around them with their","w":0.7518796793619793,"h":0.019007659465055338,"c":1},{"h":0.023933828222467701,"y":0.46047340302085904,"c":1,"t":"ability to purchase an expensive condiment from the 'exotic' East. At a banquet, a host","x":0.16715977301819721,"w":0.76531799316406246},{"w":0.77453536987304683,"h":0.019487896813013772,"c":1,"x":0.16536605166397303,"t":"would offer guests a plate with various spices piled upon it as a sign of the wealth at his","y":0.482381993634729},{"t":"or her disposal. Cinnamon was also reported to have health benefits, and was thought","y":0.50021892453489447,"x":0.1671991964980781,"w":0.76521937052408862,"h":0.020817439170783381,"c":1},{"w":0.40413533528645829,"h":0.017507375015877735,"x":0.16353383601455107,"c":1,"t":"to cure various ailments, such as indigestion.","y":0.52028332278264344},{"x":0.16534347380749675,"t":"Toward the end of the Middle Ages, the European middle classes began to desire","w":0.72006042480468757,"c":1,"y":0.55505610214801626,"h":0.020213778066543009},{"x":0.16541352934150305,"y":0.57405022521074334,"w":0.74436091105143221,"c":1,"t":"the lifestyle of the elite, including their consumption of spices. This led to a growth in","h":0.018995492594977459},{"x":0.1653580685949253,"w":0.77829371134440095,"h":0.019800585312606866,"c":1,"y":0.5913787627846151,"t":"demand for cinnamon and other spices. At that time, cinnamon was transported by Arab"},{"y":0.61043142313443677,"w":0.73872182210286452,"c":1,"x":0.16541352491213387,"h":0.017475553734872085,"t":"merchants, who closely guarded the secret of the source of the spice from potential"},{"y":0.62731340734350827,"t":"rivals. They took it from India, where it was grown, on camels via an overland route","w":0.73512573242187496,"c":1,"x":0.16345509966112881,"h":0.020567004172478032},{"t":"to the Mediterranean. Their journey ended when they reached Alexandria. European","h":0.019190965125580717,"w":0.7482731628417969,"x":0.16345287455713958,"c":1,"y":0.64600955547047112},{"t":"traders sailed there to purchase their supply of cinnamon, then brought it back to Venice.","c":1,"x":0.1634737246692661,"h":0.019737679652836126,"y":0.66402535068439317,"w":0.78771265665690104},{"t":"The spice then travelled from that great trading city to markets all around Europe.","h":0.019609386814999241,"c":1,"x":0.16532918828436133,"w":0.72009811401367196,"y":0.68237491507937964},{"h":0.019752702633181629,"t":"Because the overland trade route allowed for only small quantities of the spice to reach","w":0.77079549153645832,"x":0.16535248050740242,"c":1,"y":0.70055391357828833},{"t":"Europe, and because Venice had a virtual monopoly of the trade, the Venetians could","y":0.71947674419372076,"h":0.018895348808647183,"w":0.75563908894856779,"x":0.16541353796958808,"c":1},{"y":0.7369186046613716,"w":0.75375940958658849,"c":1,"h":0.019037609014369794,"x":0.1635338289420408,"t":"set the price of cinnamon exorbitantly high. These prices, coupled with the increasing"},{"h":0.017527965292651215,"c":1,"y":0.75581395335650114,"w":0.76315790812174478,"x":0.16353382774853609,"t":"demand, spurred the search for new routes to Asia by Europeans eager to take part in"},{"w":0.14097743988037109,"t":"the spice trade.","y":0.77462974914647098,"x":0.16353383634234769,"h":0.016097875080489321,"c":1},{"x":0.16348329651238677,"h":0.019426596371957205,"c":1,"w":0.76513214111328121,"y":0.8095664780117986,"t":"Seeking the high profits promised by the cinnamon market, Portuguese traders arrived"},{"c":1,"t":"on the island of Ceylon in the Indian Ocean toward the end of the 15th century. Before","x":0.163474359789503,"h":0.018287438234819264,"y":0.82787531011738669,"w":0.7613989257812499},{"h":0.0195334557940402,"c":1,"x":0.16532629918700034,"y":0.8453275757899168,"t":"Europeans arrived on the island, the state had organized the cultivation of cinnamon.","w":0.75205713907877614},{"y":0.86334656566411438,"h":0.019798018436468778,"x":0.16345987330259951,"c":1,"t":"People belonging to the ethnic group called the Salagama would peel the bark off","w":0.72195587158203134},{"h":0.020702701035577586,"c":1,"w":0.70691207885742202,"y":0.88118671498916079,"x":0.16345419214100265,"t":"young shoots of the cinnamon plant in the rainy season, when the wet bark was"},{"c":1,"y":0.90115904710286554,"t":"more pliable. During the peeling process, they curled the bark into the 'stick' shape","x":0.16353383678016656,"w":0.73120300292968754,"h":0.017445604185557517},{"h":0.017501759820804264,"t":"still associated with the spice today. The Salagama then gave the finished product to","x":0.16353382416747175,"w":0.74812032063802081,"y":0.91854475191707707,"c":1},{"x":0.16153724760824578,"y":0.93584644102246872,"t":"the king as a form of tribute. When the Portuguese arrived, they needed to increase","w":0.74081741333007822,"c":1,"h":0.021601842129836957},{"w":0.024436090787251813,"h":0.014534883321060788,"c":1,"x":0.16353383420380518,"y":0.96511627920914034,"t":"38"}],"w":2400,"h":3106}